From: Johannes Pletzer <johannes.pletzer@posteo.de>
Date: Wed, 16 Sep 2026 21:21:31 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 3/4] Pin the split solve on tridiagonal blocks, and take its
 iterations from the algorithm

A unit test builds a small column with two coupled scalars, a face velocity,
a tag and a record whose own blocks are tridiagonal, and solves it with the
split and the nested solver under the one- and two-iteration arrowhead solve
and the direct one. The increments agree bit for bit in every case, and a
second iteration changes the tag, so a split with the wrong count would
fail. The integration test showed neither, because its tag blocks are -I.

The split no longer takes the iteration count as a separate argument. It
reads the count and the start from the arrowhead solve own iterative
algorithm, and refuses any other algorithm. The integration comparison uses
isequal, which tells signed zeros apart.

Locally: energy source tags 229 of 229, integration 52 of 52.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
